k = y \cdot \sqrt{x} = 15 \cdot \sqrt{24}
\] Next, we need to find \(x\) when \(y = 3\). Using the same constant \(k\), we have: \[
3 \cdot \sqrt{x} = 15 \cdot \sqrt{24}
\] Solving for \(x\), we get: \[
\sqrt{x} = \frac{15 \cdot \sqrt{24}}{3} = 5 \cdot \sqrt{24} = 5 \cdot 2\sqrt{6} = 10\sqrt{6}
\] \[
x = (10\sqrt{6})^2 = 100 \cdot 6 = 600
\] So, the value of \(x\) when \(y = 3\) is \(\boxed{600}\). </think> <answer> 600 </answer>
